      "right": {
        "say": [
          "A pager. Back then half the street wore one on their belt. Someone wants you, they call the paging service with your number, and it beeps on your hip. Receives, never sends.",
          "The chick, the camera, the pager. Everything in this box is from when I was small. One at a time, in order of the years."
        ],
        "inner": "This one wasn't mine. It was my father's. My hands are a little cold. And I still want to see the next one. If it's a surprise from the family... I can't think of a single one of them who would do this."
      },
      "wrong": {
        "say": [
          "You look at it for a while. Like a phone, and not: no earpiece, no dial, only a narrow screen. You can't recall, and you don't try very hard."
